4.1
log
@WCSLIB 4.1: major changes to implement -LOG and -TAB coordinate axes, and to
implement units conversions in wcsset(); -TAB required new members of the
wcsprm struct - ntab, tab, nwtb, wtb; also added dateavg to wcsprm; set
wcs_errmsg[0] to "success"; removed support for K&R C; moved prototypes for
vector helper functions from wcs.h; changed position of crval in the wcsprm
struct for alignment; use memset() to initialize variables an wcsini(),
default value of lonpole is UNDEFINED, latpole is +90.0 (were 999.0); report
values to an extra decimal place in wcsprt(), and report all memory
management members; overhauled wcsset() to support -LOG and -TAB, making it
more general and splitting some of its functionality into new helper
functions wcs_types(), which uses new member wcsprm.types, and wcs_units()
that does units conversions based on cunit; wcsset() recognizes AIPS
spectral types, via wcs_types() and spctyp(); wcsset() resets lonpole and
latpole to the values actually used, and null-fills all string members
(mainly to prevent gdb printing garbage); new utility function wcssptr()
translates the spectral axis in a wcsprm struct.
@
